WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:11.531 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to Ukraine's regions, part 1 of 2. First, I clear the chosen names for
a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:12.197 --> 00:00:23.029 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
We work through 12 of the Ukraine regions the map names, once each: where it
sits, one fact worth keeping, and a hook to remember it by.

3
00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:25.866 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Chernihiv into view.

4
00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:59.174 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Chernihiv is in the north of Ukraine, with Russia and Belarus along its
northern edge and Kyiv Oblast, Poltava and Sumy to the south and east, and its
largest city is the town of Chernihiv.

5
00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:08.278 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its name probably comes from chornyi, black, for the dark soil or the dark
woods around the town.

6
00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:16.739 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the black north, where the Saviour Cathedral was begun before 1036,
older than anything standing in Kyiv.

7
00:01:17.838 --> 00:01:19.545 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Volyn into view.

8
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:51.993 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Volyn is in the north-west of Ukraine, with Poland and Belarus on its western
and northern edges, Lviv to the south and Rivne to the east, and Lutsk as its
largest city.

9
00:01:52.730 --> 00:02:00.730 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The name comes from the vanished town of Volyn and the Volhynians who lived
around it, a name recorded in the eleventh century.

10
00:02:01.406 --> 00:02:09.672 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the castle at Lutsk printed on the 200 hryvnia note, and the Shatsky
lakes on the Belarusian and Polish border.

11
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:13.628 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Rivne into view.

12
00:02:29.123 --> 00:02:40.977 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Rivne is in the north-west of Ukraine, with Volyn to the north-west, Zhytomyr
to the north-east, Lviv to the west and Ternopil and Khmelnytskyi to the
south, and Rivne as its largest city.

13
00:02:41.632 --> 00:02:48.157 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its name comes from rivnyi, flat or even, for the level ground around the
town.

14
00:02:49.136 --> 00:02:56.346 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the flat northern plain, where amber is dug out of the peat bog on a
scale visible from orbit.

15
00:02:57.151 --> 00:02:59.322 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Zhytomyr into view.

16
00:03:16.147 --> 00:03:29.150 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Zhytomyr is in the north of Ukraine, with Rivne to the north-west, Kyiv Oblast
to the north-east, Khmelnytskyi to the west and Vinnytsya to the south, and
Zhytomyr as its largest city.

17
00:03:29.821 --> 00:03:36.508 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Korolev, the rocket designer whose launchers carried Sputnik and Gagarin into
orbit, was born here.

18
00:03:37.163 --> 00:03:45.696 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the pink granite quarries, the largest in Ukraine, whose stone faces
buildings across the former Soviet Union.

19
00:03:46.445 --> 00:03:48.790 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Kyiv into view.

20
00:04:03.515 --> 00:04:13.709 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Kyiv is the capital of Ukraine, and the map shows it as a target in its own
right, administered separately from the Kyiv Oblast that surrounds it.

21
00:04:14.369 --> 00:04:23.285 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It was named for Kyi, the eldest of three brothers who legend says founded the
city with their sister Lybid.

22
00:04:23.976 --> 00:04:30.965 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the capital with a metro station 105 metres down through the cliffs
above the Dnipro.

23
00:04:31.916 --> 00:04:34.598 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Kyiv Oblast into view.

24
00:04:48.133 --> 00:05:00.881 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Kyiv Oblast is the region that surrounds the capital, which the map shows
separately as its own target, with Chernihiv to the north and Zhytomyr to the
west, and Bila Tserkva as its largest city.

25
00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:09.945 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Chornobyl lies in this oblast, and the exclusion zone around it has become one
of Europe’s largest wildlife refuges.

26
00:05:10.605 --> 00:05:21.182 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the ring of country round the capital, where Trypillia builders
raised settlements of fifteen thousand people around 4000 BC.

27
00:05:22.142 --> 00:05:24.696 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Lviv into view.

28
00:05:38.216 --> 00:05:55.424 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Lviv is in the west of Ukraine, with Volyn to the north, Ternopil to the east,
Ivano-Frankivsk to the south-east and Zakarpattia to the south, with Poland
beyond its western edge and Lviv as its largest city.

29
00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:09.492 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
King Danylo of Galicia founded it around 1250 and named it for his son Lev,
and it stayed Austrian until 1918 and Polish until 1939.

30
00:06:10.144 --> 00:06:18.329 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Lev’s city with more coffee houses per head than any other in
Ukraine, and a cemetery the size of Père Lachaise.

31
00:06:19.068 --> 00:06:21.831 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Khmelnytskyi into view.

32
00:06:28.159 --> 00:06:40.698 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Khmelnytskyi is in the west of Ukraine, with Rivne and Zhytomyr to the north,
Vinnytsya to the east, Ternopil to the west and Chernivtsi to the south, and
the town of Khmelnytskyy as its largest city.

33
00:06:41.347 --> 00:06:54.698 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The region was renamed in 1954 for the Cossack hetman Bohdan Khmelnytskyi,
whose uprising of 1648 created a Cossack state.

34
00:06:55.357 --> 00:07:04.018 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the western region named for the hetman, with the rock island town of
Kamianets-Podilskyi standing in a river canyon.

35
00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.737 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Ternopil into view.

36
00:07:13.468 --> 00:07:25.926 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Ternopil is a small region in the west of Ukraine, with Rivne to the north,
Lviv to the west and Ivano-Frankivsk and Chernivtsi to the south, and Ternopil
as its largest city.

37
00:07:26.609 --> 00:07:38.718 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its name means thorn field, from the blackthorn scrub the town was built on,
and the cave beneath it runs for more than 260 kilometres, the longest gypsum
cave in the world.

38
00:07:39.383 --> 00:07:47.916 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the lake dug four centuries ago as a defence, and the world’s longest
gypsum cave running under the town.

39
00:07:48.656 --> 00:07:51.419 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Ivano-Frankivsk into view.

40
00:07:58.055 --> 00:08:13.895 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Ivano-Frankivsk is in the west of Ukraine, with Lviv to the north, Ternopil to
the north-east, Zakarpattia to the west and Chernivtsi to the south. Its
largest city, Ivano-Frankivsk, is the gateway to the Carpathians.

41
00:08:14.545 --> 00:08:22.684 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The city was renamed in 1962 for the poet Ivan Franko, and for three centuries
before that it was called Stanislaviv.

42
00:08:23.342 --> 00:08:32.003 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the gateway to the Carpathians, with Hoverla, the highest mountain in
Ukraine, standing on its border with Zakarpattia.

43
00:08:32.742 --> 00:08:35.041 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Zakarpattia into view.

44
00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:53.242 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Zakarpattia is the far-western region of Ukraine, lying beyond the Carpathians
from Lviv, with Ivano-Frankivsk to the north-east and Uzhgorod as its largest
city.

45
00:08:53.892 --> 00:09:05.873 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It is the only Ukrainian region on the far side of the Carpathians, and four
countries meet along its borders, more than any other region in the country.

46
00:09:06.529 --> 00:09:15.190 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the land beyond the mountains, where Hungarian, Romanian and Rusyn
villages share the frontier with four countries.

47
00:09:15.903 --> 00:09:19.177 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Chernivtsi into view.

48
00:09:23.732 --> 00:09:37.896 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Chernivtsi is in the south-west of Ukraine, on the Prut river, with Ternopil
to the north-west, Khmelnytskyi to the north-east and Vinnytsya to the east,
and Romania lies beyond its western edge.

49
00:09:38.558 --> 00:09:52.502 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Austrian until 1918, the city was so mixed that its university was German, its
theatre Romanian and its poets, Paul Celan among them, wrote in German.

50
00:09:53.154 --> 00:10:00.573 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the university town of brick patterns and coloured roofs, a world
heritage site, named for black earth on the Prut.

51
00:10:07.122 --> 00:10:28.110 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
12 regions of Ukraine, one for each target of the map: Chernihiv, Volyn,
Rivne, Zhytomyr, Kyiv, Kyiv Oblast, Lviv, Khmelnytskyi, Ternopil,
Ivano-Frankivsk, Zakarpattia and Chernivtsi.

52
00:10:28.769 --> 00:10:38.707 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the shape of Ukraine from the inside: the regions nest around each
other, and every name on the map belongs somewhere in this one country.
